==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|peinfully}}, {{m|enm|paynefully}}, equivalent to {{af|en|painful|-ly}}.
{{PIE root|en|kʷey}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpeɪnfəli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-painfully.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[painful]] manner; as if in [[pain#Noun|pain]].
#: {{ux|en|I limped '''painfully''' down the stairs.}}
#* {{RQ:Conrad Secret Agent|chapter=IX|page=193|passage=The unsufficiency and uncandidness of his answer became '''painfully''' apparent in the dead silence of the room.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[badly|Badly]]; [[poorly]].
#: {{ux|en|That was the most '''painfully''' sung rendition of “Fly Me to the Moon” that I’ve ever heard.}}

====Usage notes====
Some adjectives commonly collocating with painfully: [[thin]], [[long]], [[slow]], [[boring]], [[close]]

